DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-long-history-of-amanuense
 s-aides-to-scholars-and-authors-from-antiquity-to-ai-6807\n\nThe technique
 s for making texts have changed across multiple media and historical conte
 xts since antiquity\, but a regular feature of the work of authors and sch
 olars through all those changes is the reliance on helpers or amanuenses. 
 Blair will discuss the factors that have made them both invisible and occa
 sionally visible\, the kind of work they did\, and offer some examples of 
 their trajectories in a few different periods. We can ponder together the 
 extent to which AI fits into and deviates from earlier patterns of assista
 nce.
